{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop (KB-021). User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, Chicago) reports leaving work laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) in an Uber last night; unsure if it was locked. Device status: ONLINE now, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:24 UTC, which is after the reported loss, so someone may have it powered on and connected. No device warnings. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 successful sign-ins, all Chicago, corporate/home residential IPs, Duo push, normal hours; latest 2026-10-08 13:23 UTC; no failures, no unfamiliar locations so far. Data at risk: logistics/operations data, cached M365 mail (mailbox 99.4% full, ~50 GB, likely large local cache), saved VPN access. Action taken: block_sign_in queued for tech approval (approval id 1). Needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 while it is online, revoke sessions/tokens, password reset after identity verification by phone, replacement device. I have asked the user for when/where it was last seen and to report it to Uber.",
  "reason": "KB-021 says always escalate lost devices for remote lock/wipe; P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for telling us so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. Here's where things stand: (1) I've asked for your work sign-in to be blocked so nobody can use anything saved on the laptop. A technician has to approve this first. Once they do, you won't be able to sign in anywhere for a while, and we'll call you to verify who you are and set up a new password. (2) I've passed this to our senior team so they can lock or wipe the laptop remotely and arrange a replacement. Please reply with when and where you last had the laptop (roughly what time and which ride), and whether you remember signing out or closing the lid. Please also report it as lost in the Uber app so the driver can return it. If you think it was stolen and not just left behind, please file a police report and send us the report number. Don't worry if the laptop turns up, just let us know right away.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 P1. User 9 has one device, BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15). It is ONLINE with last check-in 2026-10-09 14:24 UTC, after the reported loss last night, so it is powered on somewhere. Sign-in logs show nothing suspicious so far: all Chicago corporate/home IPs, Duo push, normal hours, latest 2026-10-08 13:23 UTC, no failures. Lock status is unknown, so per KB-021 I queued block_sign_in (approval id 1, NOT yet run). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for remote lock/wipe while the device is online, session/token revocation and a replacement. Still to do: reset the password after phone verification. Note the mailbox is 99.4% full, so the laptop likely holds a large local mail cache. Asked the user where and when it was last seen, plus a police report if stolen.",
